{
  "id": "29983_ensuto",
  "headword": "エンスト",
  "reading": "えんすと",
  "romaji": "ensuto",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "engine stall",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "engine stall; stalling of the engine",
      "explanation": "An unintended stopping of a car's engine while driving or maneuvering, typically from mishandling the clutch. A {和製英語|わせいえいご} clipping of \"engine stop\" (エンジンストップ). Takes する."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29983_ensuto_ex1",
      "japanese": "エンストした。",
      "english": "The engine stalled.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29983_ensuto_ex2",
      "japanese": "{交差点|こうさてん}でエンストしてしまった。",
      "english": "I stalled the car at the intersection.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29983_ensuto_ex3",
      "japanese": "クラッチ{操作|そうさ}に{慣|な}れないうちは{坂道|さかみち}でエンストしやすい。",
      "english": "Until you get used to the clutch, it is easy to stall on a hill.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Mostly associated with manual-transmission cars, where clutch mistakes cut the engine.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- エンストする: to stall the engine\n- エンストを{起|お}こす: to have a stall\n- {坂道|さかみち}でエンストする: to stall on a hill\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {故障|こしょう}: breakdown — an actual mechanical failure, whereas an エンスト is usually just an operating mistake",
